  "title": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (9.31g), Peshawar, VS1891//1891",
  "description": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (9.31g), Peshawar, VS1891//1891, KM-98.1, Herrli-13.01.04, without the border of dots around the pipal leaf, nice strike, About VF, RR.  Both Herrli & KM failed to note that the variety without the dots is heavier, about 9.3g, instead of 8.5g, thus equal to the standard of the last Durrani rupees of Peshawar struck during the previous year (AH1249). The dots were presumably added to indicate the reduced weight (see our comment to lot 1259 in our auction 14). Like so many pre-machine-struck rupees, this example was blackened and then lightly scraped to create the appearance of white text on a black background.",
